  clock: 4  # 3a7c
  nonce: 3a7c  # 3a7c
  message: "2026-09-18, a sibling of this row's shape was found and fixed in the SCIP arm\n(INV-mofiv, PR #1047): every SCIP occurrence-ref edge was sourced from the\nFILE's module namespace and none from the enclosing callable, because the\nshim enclosed by the Definition's identifier-token `range` and ignored the\npopulated item-range `enclosing_range`. Fix: use the emitter-supplied extent;\nmethod-sourced edges 0 -> 287 on aardvark-dns. This row (io_edge_src anchored\nto a FILE node, 194 chains) is the same \"anchored to the file, not the\ncallable\" defect in the I/O-boundary pipeline; the mechanism there is\ndifferent and this note does not claim the SCIP fix reaches it. Not started."  # 3a7c
- op: discuss  # 3836
  at: '2026-09-25T17:56:46Z'  # 3836
  by: agent  # 3836
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3836
  clock: 5  # 3836
  nonce: '3836'  # 3836
  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). RE-MEASURED; the population has a different composition from the one filed. Status unchanged.\n\nInstrument: fresh `hypergumbo survey .` of this repo at dev (53,828 nodes), then `hypergumbo io-boundaries --input <it> --format json` (production-only default). Each chain's io_edge_src was joined to its node kind. Then the survey edges between (io_edge_src, io_edge_dst) were classified by type.\n\n  chains 2,290; io_edge_src kind: function 1,719 · FILE 394 (17.2%) · method 177.\n\nThe 394 FILE-anchored chains, by (language, edge type behind the chain):\n  bash   calls            202   top-level script commands. The file IS the enclosing scope, since there is no callable, and INV-nopoh's module-level anchoring makes the file pseudo-symbol the correct src.\n  bash   module_attr_ref   25   same, for reads.\n  python IMPORTS          118   the chain rides an `imports` edge (file -> imported I/O primitive, e.g. a function-local `import time` or `from importlib.metadata import version`). Imports are file-sourced BY DESIGN. Here the io layer counts the IMPORT of a primitive as an I/O chain.\n  python calls             30   not individually adjudicated. These are the only candidates for the filed shape (a call inside a callable anchored to the file).\n  python module_attr_ref   19   not adjudicated.\n\nWHAT THIS CHANGES:\n(1) The row's Expectation (\"resolve io_edge_src to the enclosing callable\") does not apply to the 227 bash rows, which have no enclosing callable.\n(2) The largest Python sub-shape is not an anchoring defect at all but a CLASSIFICATION one: an `imports` edge admitted as an I/O chain. The 118 are likely also double-counted alongside the call-sourced chain from the function that actually calls the primitive. NOT verified per row.\n(3) The filed shape itself is bounded above by 49 (python calls + module_attr_ref) on this corpus and was not adjudicated.\n\nRecommend re-scoping before work starts: split \"imports edge admitted as an I/O chain\" out as its own row. The owner may prefer the split to be decided first."  # 3836
